<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
    <dict>
        <key>Description</key>
        <string>This download is NOT verified yet: Google publishes no hash for the file, and the shared signature check (AuthenticodeVerifier) is not part of this recipe, so nothing proves that the file is what Google published. The shared importer therefore refuses a real run of the cimian recipe unless the override sets cimian_allow_unverified to true (pcman_allow_unverified for the package tool's recipe). Downloads the current Google Credential Provider for Windows enterprise installer (the 64-bit MSI that Google serves at a fixed address), kept under the file name of the address. The address and the size of the file were read by the writer on 2026-10-02, but this recipe was NOT rehearsed with AutoPkg: the first run on the build machine is the check of the rest. The recipe never stops on an unchanged download, so a failed import is tried again at the next run.</string>
        <key>Identifier</key>
        <string>com.github.serrc-techops.download.GCPW-Win</string>
        <key>Input</key>
        <dict>
            <key>NAME</key>
            <string>GCPW</string>
            <key>DOWNLOAD_URL</key>
            <string>https://dl.google.com/credentialprovider/gcpwstandaloneenterprise64.msi</string>
        </dict>
        <key>MinimumVersion</key>
        <string>1.0.0</string>
        <key>Process</key>
        <array>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>URLDownloader</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>url</key>
                    <string>%DOWNLOAD_URL%</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>EndOfCheckPhase</string>
            </dict>
        </array>
    </dict>
</plist>
